<p>I feel like gaw is at its best when really exploring their characters. I was interested in where this was going to head initially, but ended up seeming vapid and unfulfilling.</p>
<p>There's nothing really interesting about the item (it's about as vanilla as they come), so I can't really even appreciate it for what it is.</p>
<p>The final interaction, given that any history or buildup is relayed to an afterthought of a footnote, falls completely flat; making it feel inauthentic and ultimately meaningless.</p>
<p>This especially, feels like its getting around characterization via tell over show:</p>
